<h2 id="connect-the-badge">1. Connect the badge</h2>

<p>
  Connect the badge to your computer with a USB cable that transfers data.
  Leave it connected while Copilot works. You do not need to enter Disk Mode
  before you start.
</p>

<p>
  When Copilot is ready to copy your app, <code>hyb26-skill</code> switches
  the badge into <strong>USB Disk Mode</strong>. The badge restarts and
  appears as a <strong>BADGER</strong> drive on your computer. This is expected.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>If automatic Disk Mode fails:</strong> quickly press
  <strong>RESET</strong> twice, then ask Copilot to try again.
  If it still cannot find BADGER, check the USB data cable and ask staff for help.
</p>

<p>
  If you see <strong>RP2350</strong>, stop: that drive is for firmware updates,
  not apps. Do not copy files to it, erase the drive, or change the firmware.
</p>
